{{also|devanagari|devanágari|Dēvanāgarī}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|en}} {{m|sa|देवनागरी}}, compound of {{m|sa|देव||deity, divine}} + {{m|sa|नगर||town, city}}.<!--The name Devanagari should therefore be understood as “excellent or perfected form of the Nagari script”.-->

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌdeɪvəˈnɑːɡəɹiː/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-Devanagari.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of the Devanagari script or of a Devanagari alphabet.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|-}}

# An [[abugida]] script used to write several [[Indian]] languages, mainly [[Sanskrit]] and [[Hindi]], but also [[Marathi]], [[Kashmiri]], [[Sindhi]], [[Bihari]], [[Bhili]], [[Konkani]], and [[Bhojpuri]]. It is also used to write [[Nepali]] in [[Nepal]].

